---
description: Use string resources for all user-facing text (en/ar)
globs: "**/*.kt", "**/res/values/**/strings.xml"
alwaysApply: false
---

# String resources (i18n)

- **No hardcoded user-facing text** in Composables or View code. Use `stringResource(R.string.xxx)` (Compose) or `context.getString(R.string.xxx)` so the app can ship **en** and **ar** (and other locales) from `values/strings.xml` and `values-ar/strings.xml`.
- **Add every new UI string** to the appropriate `strings.xml` (app or core/designsystem) and to `values-ar/strings.xml` for Arabic.
- **Parameterized strings**: use format args, e.g. `stringResource(R.string.home_hi, userName)` with `<string name="home_hi">Hi, %1$s</string>`.
- **Content descriptions**: use string resources for `contentDescription` (e.g. `stringResource(R.string.home_menu_cd)`), not inline literals.

```kotlin
// BAD
Text("Your Streak")
Icon(..., contentDescription = "Menu")

// GOOD
Text(stringResource(R.string.home_your_streak))
Icon(..., contentDescription = stringResource(R.string.home_menu_cd))
```
